.Dd April 22, 2026
.Dt MKIT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mkit
.Nd decentralized, content-addressed version control with cryptographic attribution
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a git-like command-line tool that produces signed, content-addressed
objects and exchanges them over pluggable transports
.Pq Cm mkit+file , Cm mkit+https , Cm mkit+s3 , Cm mkit+ssh .
Every commit is Ed25519-signed and identified by its BLAKE3 hash, so
chains of objects are self-verifying independent of the store they live
in.
.Pp
The on-disk layout under
.Pa .mkit/
is deliberately similar to
.Pa .git/ :
objects are stored under
.Pa .mkit/objects/ ,
refs under
.Pa .mkit/refs/ ,
and the current branch is recorded in
.Pa .mkit/HEAD .
A user-level config at
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mkit/config
provides cross-repo defaults; repo-local values in
.Pa .mkit/config
always win.
.Sh COMMANDS
The full list of subcommands is printed by
.Nm mkit Fl Fl help .
The highlights:
.Bl -tag -width "cherry-pick"
.It Cm init
Create a new
.Nm
repository in the current directory.
.It Cm add Oo Fl A | Fl Fl all Oc Oo Fl u | Fl Fl update Oc Ar path ...
Stage files for the next commit. Respects
.Pa .mkitignore .
Multiple pathspecs may be given;
.Ql .
stages every non-ignored file under the current directory.
.Fl A
or
.Fl Fl all
stages every worktree change including deletions of tracked files (takes no
path arguments).
.Fl u
or
.Fl Fl update
restages only already-tracked files \(em updating modified ones and recording
deletions \(em without adding untracked paths (takes no path arguments).
.Fl A
and
.Fl u
are mutually exclusive. Interactive hunk staging
.Pq Fl p
is not supported.
.It Cm rm Oo Fl Fl cached Oc Oo Fl r | Fl Fl recursive Oc Oo Fl f | Fl Fl force Oc Ar path ...
Remove paths and stage the deletion for the next commit. By default this
deletes the worktree file(s) and prunes now-empty parent directories.
Multiple pathspecs are accepted.
.Fl Fl cached
stages the removal only, keeping the worktree file(s).
.Fl r
or
.Fl Fl recursive
is required to remove a directory and everything under it.
.Fl f
or
.Fl Fl force
removes files even when their worktree content has diverged from the staged
blob; without it,
.Cm rm
refuses to destroy a locally-modified tracked file.
.It Cm restore Oo Fl Fl staged Oc Oo Fl Fl worktree Oc Oo Fl Fl source Ar rev Oc Oo Fl f | Fl Fl force Oc Ar path ...
Restore path(s) in the worktree and/or unstage them. With no flag (or
.Fl Fl worktree ) ,
the worktree file(s) are rewritten from the staged index content,
discarding un-staged worktree edits.
.Fl Fl staged
instead reverts the index entry for each path to its
.Cm HEAD
version (unstaging it) while leaving the worktree file untouched;
.Fl Fl staged Fl Fl worktree
does both. A directory path restores every tracked entry at or below it.
.Fl Fl source Ar rev
takes the restored content from
.Ar rev Ns 's
tree (resolved as a branch, tag,
.Cm HEAD ,
full or short hash, or
.Cm HEAD~ Ns Ar n Ns / Ns Cm ^
navigation) instead of the index/HEAD default. The worktree restore
refuses to overwrite a file whose content diverges from the staged blob;
.Fl f
or
.Fl Fl force
discards that un-staged edit. A worktree restore never removes neighbouring
files \(em it only rewrites the named tracked paths.
.It Cm reset Oo Fl Fl soft | Fl Fl mixed Oc Op Ar commit
Move
.Cm HEAD
.Pq and the current branch
to
.Ar commit
.Pq default Cm HEAD ,
resolved through the shared revision grammar (branch, tag,
.Cm HEAD ,
full or short hash,
.Cm HEAD~ Ns Ar n Ns / Ns Cm ^ ) .
.Fl Fl soft
moves
.Cm HEAD
only, leaving the index and worktree untouched.
.Fl Fl mixed
.Pq the default
also resets the index to the target commit's tree while leaving the
worktree. The destructive
.Fl Fl hard
variant
.Pq also resetting the worktree
is intentionally not implemented;
.Cm checkout Ar commit
provides a guarded worktree-resetting path instead.
.It Cm hash Ar file
Hash
.Ar file
as a blob, store it under
.Pa .mkit/objects/ ,
and print the resulting BLAKE3 hash on stdout.
.It Cm cat Ar hash
Decode and print the object identified by
.Ar hash
on stdout.
.It Cm tree
Snapshot the working directory as a tree object and print the tree hash.
Honors
.Pa .mkitignore
the same way
.Cm add
does.
.It Cm commit Op Fl a | Fl Fl all Op Fl m Ar message
Create a signed commit. With
.Fl a
or
.Fl Fl all ,
first stage modified tracked files and tracked deletions, but do not add
untracked files. The combined
.Fl am Ar message
form is accepted as shorthand for
.Fl a Fl m Ar message .
If
.Fl m
is omitted,
.Nm
opens
.Ev EDITOR
on
.Pa .mkit/COMMIT_EDITMSG ;
lines starting with
.Ql #
are stripped, and an empty message aborts the commit.
.It Cm log Op Fl Fl oneline Op Fl Fl format Ar json Op Fl Fl graph Op Fl n Ar N
Show commit history. The default format prints the full commit message body,
indented by four spaces, and renders the timestamp as a stable UTC date in the
form
.Ql YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS +0000 .
.Fl Fl oneline
condenses each commit to
.Ql <8-hex> <title> .
.Fl Fl format Ar json
emits one JSON object per commit on stdout, keeping the raw integer Unix
timestamp for machine consumption.
.Fl Fl graph
is accepted for compatibility but is currently a no-op (no ASCII graph is
drawn).
.It Cm diff Oo Fl Fl staged | Fl Fl cached Oc Oo Ar treeA Ar treeB Oc Ar path ...
Show changes as a unified patch. With no arguments, compares the HEAD tree to
a fresh worktree snapshot.
.Fl Fl staged
.Pq alias Fl Fl cached
compares the HEAD tree to the staged index tree. Two 64-hex tree hashes diff
those trees directly. Remaining positional arguments are pathspecs that limit
the output. Commit-vs-commit diffing takes two
.Em tree
hashes, not commit refs or ranges.
.It Cm status Oo Fl Fl porcelain Oc Oo Fl s | Fl Fl short Oc
Show the staged and working-tree changes.
.Fl s
.Pq alias Fl Fl short
is equivalent to
.Fl Fl porcelain Ns = Ns Cm v1 :
both emit machine-readable XY-code-plus-path lines on stdout. There is no
.Fl z
NUL-termination or path-quoting support.
.It Cm branch Oo Fl d | Fl D | Fl m Oc Op Ar name ...
List, create, rename, or delete branches. With no arguments, lists
branches.  With one
.Ar name ,
creates a branch at HEAD.
.Fl d
deletes a branch (refuses the current branch);
.Fl D
force-deletes (an absent branch is a clean no-op, but the current branch
is still refused).
.Fl m Oo Ar old Oc Ar new
renames a branch \(em the current branch when
.Ar old
is omitted \(em and moves HEAD if the renamed branch is checked out.
.It Cm checkout Ar branch
Switch HEAD to a branch and restore files from its tree.
.It Cm tag Oo Ar name Oc Op Fl d Ar name
List, create, or delete tags. With no arguments, prints the list of
tags. With a
.Ar name
argument, creates a tag at HEAD. With
.Fl d ,
deletes the named tag.
.It Cm sparse-checkout Cm set | Cm list | Cm disable | Cm reapply Op Ar pattern ...
Manage the sparse-checkout pattern set at
.Pa .mkit/sparse-checkout .
.Cm set
overwrites the pattern list,
.Cm list
prints the current patterns,
.Cm disable
clears them, and
.Cm reapply
re-materialises the working tree from the current patterns.
.It Cm merge Ar branch
Merge
.Ar branch
into HEAD. Fast-forwards when possible.
.It Cm rebase Ar branch
Replay commits from HEAD onto
.Ar branch .
Accepts
.Fl Fl continue
and
.Fl Fl abort
after a conflict.
.It Cm push Op Fl Fl dry-run
Push HEAD's commit chain to the configured remote.
.It Cm pull , Cm fetch
Download or download-and-merge from the remote.
.It Cm clone Op Fl Fl depth Ar N Op Fl Fl sparse ... Ar url
Clone a remote into a new working directory.
.It Cm remote Oo Cm add | Cm set | Cm remove | Cm rename Oc Op Ar args ...
Show or configure remotes. With no subcommand, lists the configured
remotes.
.Cm add
(alias
.Cm set )
adds the flat default remote
.Pq Cm remote add Ar url
or a named remote
.Pq Cm remote add Ar name url ;
URLs MUST use the strict
.Ql mkit+<scheme>://
form.
.Cm remove Ar name
.Pq alias Cm rm
deletes a named remote
.Pq the reserved Ar default No name clears the flat remote ;
.Cm rename Ar old new
.Pq alias Cm mv
renames a named remote and repoints any branch upstream tracking it.
Removing or renaming a remote never touches the user-scoped
.Ar trusted_remote_endpoint ,
which is keyed by exact URL rather than remote name.
.It Cm cherry-pick Ar hash
Apply a single commit from elsewhere onto HEAD.
.It Cm bisect Cm start | Cm good | Cm bad | Cm reset
Binary-search for the commit that introduced a regression.
.It Cm stash Op Cm save Fl m Ar msg | Cm list | Cm pop Op Ar N | Cm apply Op Ar N | Cm drop Op Ar N | Cm clear | Cm show Op Ar N
Save or restore a snapshot of working-tree changes.
.Cm pop
applies entry
.Ar N
and removes it;
.Cm apply
applies entry
.Ar N
but leaves it on the stack. Both run the destructive-restore guard so
uncommitted edits on unrelated paths are never clobbered.
.Cm clear
removes every stash entry.
.It Cm blame Ar file
Line-level attribution of the committed state of
.Ar file .
.It Cm verify Ar hash
Verify the signature on a commit object.
.It Cm attest Oo Fl Fl commit Ar hash Oc Op Fl Fl algorithm Ar alg Op Fl Fl signer Ar kind Op Fl Fl predicate-type Ar uri Op Fl Fl predicate-file Ar path
Produce a signed DSSE attestation for the given commit (defaults to
HEAD). Multiple
.Fl Fl additional-signer
specs may be supplied to co-sign the attestation. The resulting
envelope is attached to the commit's attestation set.
.It Cm verify-attest Oo Fl Fl commit Ar hash Oc Op Fl Fl trust-roots Ar path Op Fl Fl algorithm Ar filter
Verify every attestation attached to the given commit. Returns success
only if every envelope verifies; an algorithm filter restricts the
check to a single algorithm.
.It Cm key Cm generate | Cm list | Cm import | Cm export | Cm delete
Manage user-scoped keystore keys backed by the platform keystore
(Keychain on macOS, libsecret/systemd-creds/YubiKey on Linux, Credential
Manager on Windows). Unlike
.Cm keygen
(which writes to a repo-local file), these keys persist across repos.
.It Cm keygen
Generate a fresh Ed25519 keypair in
.Pa .mkit/keys/default.key .
.It Cm config Ar key Op Ar value
Read or write a config key. Recognized keys include
.Cm user.identity , Cm ssh.strict_host_key_checking ,
.Cm ssh.user_known_hosts_file ,
and
.Cm ssh.identity_file .
.It Cm serve Ar path
Internal subcommand: act as the server end of an
.Cm mkit+ssh://
transport.
.It Cm version
Print the version to stdout as
.Ql mkit <X.Y.Z> .
This is the canonical version query: there is no top-level
.Fl Fl version
flag.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "CLICOLOR_FORCE"
.It Ev EDITOR , Ev VISUAL
Editor used by
.Cm mkit commit
when no
.Fl m
is supplied. If neither is set, the commit aborts with a clear error.
.It Ev NO_COLOR
If set to any value (including empty),
.Nm
suppresses ANSI color output on stdout. See
.Lk https://no-color.org .
.It Ev CLICOLOR_FORCE
If set to
.Ql 1 ,
.Nm
emits ANSI color even when stdout is not a terminal.
.Ev NO_COLOR
overrides this.
.It Ev SSH_AUTH_SOCK
Standard OpenSSH agent socket; used when pushing or cloning via
.Cm mkit+ssh:// .
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME , Ev XDG_DATA_HOME , Ev XDG_CACHE_HOME , Ev XDG_STATE_HOME
Locations of user-level config, keystore, cache, and state
respectively. See
.Sx FILES .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.local/state/mkit/"
.It Pa .mkit/
Repo-local state dir (analogous to
.Pa .git/ ).
.It Pa .mkit/config
Repo-local config; overrides any user-level value.
.It Pa .mkit/keys/default.key
Repo-local Ed25519 signing key.
.It Pa .mkit/index
Staged-change index.
.It Pa .mkit/index.lock
Lockfile held by
.Cm commit , Cm checkout , Cm merge , Cm rebase
to serialize concurrent invocations.
.It Pa .mkit/COMMIT_EDITMSG
Scratch file written before
.Ev EDITOR
is invoked by
.Cm commit .
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mkit/config
User-level config.
.It Pa $XDG_DATA_HOME/mkit/keys/
User-level keystore (optional; for a single identity across repos).
.It Pa $XDG_CACHE_HOME/mkit/
User-level cache directory.
.It Pa $XDG_STATE_HOME/mkit/
User-level state directory.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
follows the BSD
.Xr sysexits 3
conventions where practical:
.Bl -tag -width "76"
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
General error (catch-all).
.It 64
Command-line usage error (unknown subcommand, missing required arg).
.It 65
Input data was malformed (corrupt object, bad hex hash).
.It 66
Input file was missing or unreadable.
.It 69
Service unavailable (transport could not connect).
.It 73
Could not create output (permission denied writing a ref, etc.).
.It 75
Temporary failure; retrying is safe (5xx after retry budget,
SIGINT/SIGTERM interruption).
.It 76
Protocol error (bad URL scheme, malformed server response).
.It 77
Permission denied.
.It 78
Config error (unknown key, invalid value).
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Errors are written to stderr on a single line beginning with
.Ql error: .
When
.Ev NO_COLOR
is unset and stdout is a terminal, colored labels may be used; consult
.Ev CLICOLOR_FORCE
to override.
.Pp
.Nm
installs
.Dv SIGPIPE
as ignored, so common pipelines like
.Dl mkit log | head -1
exit cleanly without a "Broken pipe" message.
.Dv SIGINT
and
.Dv SIGTERM
set a flag that long-running operations honor at the next checkpoint.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr sysexits 3
.Pp
Project documentation lives alongside the source under
.Pa docs/ ;
see
.Pa docs/CLI.md
for a short usage reference and
.Pa docs/SPEC-OBJECTS.md
et al. for the on-disk format.
